Four files in this repository are derivative works of RLinf: the stochastic sampler for flow matching policies
(src/flow_sde.py), the critic head (src/value_head.py), the policy gradient update (src/ppo_step.py), and the
wrapper that gives the pretrained policy the pieces a policy gradient needs (src/action_model.py). Two of those
four, src/flow_sde.py and src/action_model.py, have LeRobot as a second upstream and are described again in the
LeRobot entry below. They derive principally from rlinf/models/embodiment/openpi/openpi_action_model.py and
rlinf/models/embodiment/modules/value_head.py. Every file containing adapted material carries a notice of
modification in its header, as required by Section 4(b) of the Apache License, and retains the copyright line
above, as required by Section 4(c). The full licence text is in the LICENSE file at the root of this repository.

The revision is pinned because an unpinned reference to a file path is not a reference at all: upstream headers
change, and a retained copyright line that was correct when it was written silently stops matching. Both files
named above carry "Copyright 2025 The RLinf Authors." at the pinned commit, which is the line retained here. A
later upstream revision may carry a different year; readers comparing against upstream should compare against
the pinned commit.

Section 4(d) does not apply: the RLinf distribution contains no NOTICE file at that revision, and no AUTHORS or
COPYRIGHT file either. Established by listing the distribution root rather than assumed.

Section 4(c) was checked over the whole of both upstream files rather than over their headers. Each carries
exactly one copyright line, the one reproduced above, and no further attribution notice anywhere in its 1392 and
67 lines respectively. This was worth checking rather than assuming because one of them sits in a directory named
after a separate Apache licensed project: it imports that project as a dependency, which creates no obligation
here, and this repository imports nothing from it.

