Both a dependency and an upstream.

As a dependency, this repository imports LeRobot for the policy implementation, the observation preprocessing
utilities and the simulator environment factory.

As an upstream, two files are derivative works, and both draw on lerobot/policies/smolvla/modeling_smolvla.py:

- src/action_model.py, whose prefix cache construction follows that file's own closely.
- src/flow_sde.py, whose integration grid and deterministic Euler step are that file's constant step expression.

Both carry their own notice of modification under Section 4(b) and retain the copyright line above under Section
4(c), which is the line that file carries at version 0.4.4. No verbatim LeRobot source file is redistributed here.

Section 4(d) does not apply: the LeRobot distribution contains no NOTICE file at that version. Checked, not
assumed, the same way it was checked for RLinf.

Section 4(c) was also considered for the attribution notices embedded inside LeRobot's own LICENSE file, which is
not the plain Apache text: it carries four MIT notices, for work by the Columbia Artificial Intelligence and
Robotics Lab, by Yunhai Feng, by Nicklas Hansen and Yanjie Ze, and by Tony Z. Zhao, and a second Apache licence
for work by Facebook. Section 4(c) requires retaining attribution notices from the Source form except those that
do not pertain to any part of the Derivative Works. The test is applied to the Derivative Works, not to the
upstream file, and the distinction matters here: one of the five does pertain to the upstream file. The SmolVLA
policy implementation carries Aloha derived gripper conversions and says so in its own comments, which is the work
the Tony Z. Zhao notice covers. It pertains to no part of what is derived here. Neither src/action_model.py nor
src/flow_sde.py contains any of that material, established by searching both for it rather than by assuming it.
The other four pertain to neither. So none is reproduced, and the reasoning is recorded rather than left implicit,
because a reader cannot otherwise tell a determination from an omission.

Section 4(c) was also checked over the whole of modeling_smolvla.py rather than over its header, the same way it
was checked for RLinf, and there were two things in that file to find. The helper make_att_2d_masks opens with
"Copied from big_vision", which is Google Research work under its own Apache licence; it is not reproduced here
because src/action_model.py imports that function from LeRobot rather than carrying a copy of it, so its body is
not part of the Derivative Works. And the Aloha derived gripper conversions attribute their constants to the
Interbotix code in their own comments; that block is the same material the Tony Z. Zhao notice covers, and it is
absent from both derivative files, which was checked by searching them for it. Both are recorded because the
alternative is a reader finding a notice themselves and having no way to tell whether it was considered.

LeRobot's LICENSE file itself opens with a project level line, "Copyright 2024 The Hugging Face team. All rights
reserved.", which differs in year and in entity form from the per file line retained above. That line is in the
licence file and not in the source file: the policy implementation carries only the 2025 per file form. The per
file line is the one reproduced, because Section 4(c) speaks of the notices carried by the Source form of the
work that was derived from, and that is `modeling_smolvla.py`, whose own header states the 2025 form. It was
read byte for byte from the installed distribution. The project level line is recorded here so that a reader
comparing the two does not have to guess which was chosen or why.

