The revision is recorded for the same reason the code upstreams are pinned above: a licence quoted from a target
that can move is not a quotation. This is also the only kind of entry in this file where this repository asserts
somebody else's grant rather than reproducing a licence text it ships, so it is the one that most needs a date.

These weights are a fine tune of lerobot/smolvla_base, which states no licence on its own model card. The grant
above is the one the fine tuned repository states; a reader who needs a clean chain of title further upstream
should know that the base states none. Recorded because this is the material fact about these weights and the
rest of this entry would otherwise read as though the two were unrelated checkpoints.

Not distributed here. The helper in scripts/ downloads them from the Hub at the user's own request. This is the
default because it is the policy this harness can actually drive: the generic base checkpoint declares different
camera keys and different state and action widths, so it cannot be used here at all.

