Backbone weights
Repository: HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct on the Hugging Face Hub
https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-500M-Video-Instruct
Revision read: 7b375e1b73b11138ff12fe22c8f2822d8fe03467, read on 2026-07-27.

Licence: Apache License, Version 2.0, as stated on the model card at that revision.

The default policy's configuration asks for HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-500M-Instruct, which the Hub redirects to the
repository named above; both names return that same revision, the same files and the same licence. The generic
SmolVLA base names the canonical form directly. The revision and the licence here were read on the canonical
repository, since a name that resolves by redirect is the moving target this file elsewhere says it pins against.

Not distributed here. The helper in scripts/ reads the backbone repository out of the downloaded policy's own
configuration and fetches that, rather than carrying a name of its own. That is a precaution rather than a
demonstrated need: the two names seen so far resolve to one repository, but a checkpoint is free to ask for a
different backbone, and a name written into a script is right for the policy it was written against and silently
wrong for the next one.
A policy fetched with a different --repo therefore brings its own backbone, whose terms this file does not state.
